        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add windowsHide true to SDK terminal command spawning",
        "summary": "Added windowsHide: true to child process options in run-terminal-command.ts. Prevents Windows console-attached descendants from stealing VT input from the TUI's ConPTY, eliminating gibberish echoes like ^[[I^[[<35;12;7M. Scope limited to SDK terminal tool execution.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T15:55:02.356Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When the assistant runs a command in your terminal on Windows, it now hides the extra console window that used to pop up alongside it. That stray window was letting programs like Command Prompt or PowerShell peek at the terminal's hidden input stream and print garbled codes like ^[[I^[[<35;12;7M over the screen. You would notice fewer random characters appearing on top of your terminal interface while commands run. The fix is live today and applies only to terminal commands the assistant launches on Windows.",
